  <section class="vt-why">
    <div class="vt-why__inner">
      <div class="vt-why__media">
        <img
          src="/images/vista-window-film-philadelphia-why.jpg"
          alt="Philadelphia building interior with bright glass suited for Vista architectural film"
          title="Philadelphia buildings suited for Vista architectural window film"
          width="848"
          height="1264"
          loading="lazy"
          class="vt-why__img"
        />
        <div class="vt-why__stat-card">
          <strong>IECC Climate Zone 4A</strong>
          <span>4 full seasons</span>
          <small>~2,500 sunshine hours per year</small>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="vt-why__content">
        <span class="vt-why__eyebrow">Designed for demanding glass</span>
        <h2 class="vt-why__title">Philadelphia's Design-Forward Buildings Need a Film That Performs and Disappears</h2>
        <p class="vt-why__intro">Philadelphia sits in IECC Climate Zone 4A — genuine summers and genuine winters that stress both commercial HVAC systems and aging residential glass. Vista film installer for Philadelphia projects is chosen when performance is non-negotiable and appearance matters equally: the SpectraSelect Series maintains a near-neutral exterior look that meets historic district requirements in Society Hill, Chestnut Hill, and Fairmount while still rejecting meaningful solar heat on south- and west-facing glazing.</p>
        <ul class="vt-why__bullets">
          <li><Icon name="lucide:home" aria-hidden="true" />Aging single-pane rowhome glass loses heat in winter — Vista Low-E adds insulating performance without altering the window's appearance</li>
          <li><Icon name="lucide:building-2" aria-hidden="true" />Center City offices with floor-to-ceiling glass face intense solar gain — Vista SpectraSelect rejects up to 71% of solar heat while preserving views and daylight</li>
          <li><Icon name="lucide:shield-check" aria-hidden="true" />Healthcare facilities and universities need film with documented safety performance — Vista SpectraSelect Safety addresses solar control and fragment retention in one product</li>
          <li><Icon name="lucide:file-check-2" aria-hidden="true" />All Vista films are NFRC-certified for VLT, SHGC, and U-value — meeting documentation requirements for LEED and institutional procurement</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="vt-why__closing">"Vista architectural window film is engineered for demanding commercial applications where performance, aesthetics, and documentation all matter," according to Vista by Eastman. For energy reduction strategies beyond window film, explore our <a href="/benefits/energy-savings/">energy savings window film</a> page. Homeowners can find residential-specific options on our <a href="/applications/homes-condos/">residential window film</a> page. For commercial specifications, see our <a href="/applications/office/">commercial office window film</a> page. Review the full <a href="https://www.llumar.com/en/coverage/architectural-film/vista-window-film/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Vista architectural film overview</a> for product documentation.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="vt-why__facts" aria-label="Philadelphia climate facts">
      <div><strong>2,500</strong><span>Sunshine hours per year</span></div>
      <div><strong>87°F</strong><span>Average July high</span></div>
      <div><strong>Zone 4A</strong><span>Mixed-humid, 4 seasons</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="vt-slider" aria-labelledby="vt-slider-title">
    <div class="vt-slider__header">
      <span class="vt-slider__eyebrow">Residential and commercial Vista applications</span>
      <h2 id="vt-slider-title" class="vt-slider__title">Two Ways Philadelphia Buildings Use Vista</h2>
      <div class="vt-slider__nav">
        <button class="vt-slider__button" type="button" data-vtnav="prev" aria-label="Previous slide"><Icon name="lucide:arrow-left" aria-hidden="true" /></button>
        <button class="vt-slider__button" type="button" data-vtnav="next" aria-label="Next slide"><Icon name="lucide:arrow-right" aria-hidden="true" /></button>
      </div>
